==Trivia==
*The word Gaō in Commander Hannya's Japanese name, Bushō Hannya Gaō (武将般若我王), doesn't mean anything on its own and is just a pun on ''kao'' (顔), meaning "face", though it can rarely also be a person's name. It consists of the kanji for "ego" or "self-assertion" (我) and "king" (王).
*The helmet and eyepatch are likely a reference to [[wikipedia:Date Masamune|Date Masamune]], a sengoku warlord who is usually portrayed wearing a kabuto with a crescent shaped horn, and an eyepatch.

